# MAIW Preflight Sync

At the start of any substantive work in this workspace, refresh code context before relying on
memory or making changes.

Default preflight:
- Pull the MAIW wrapper repo first.
- Pull the relevant nested app repo(s) under `apps/` before coding, debugging, reviewing, or
  planning implementation details.
- If an app repo moved, sync that app's memory before treating `memory/<app>/NOW.md` and topics as
  current.

Safety rules:
- Do this proactively; do not wait for the user to ask.
- If local uncommitted changes would make pull risky, stop and tell the user what is dirty instead
  of auto-merging or stashing.
- Never overwrite local changes, reset branches, or change git identity during preflight.

Preferred commands:
- Use `git pull` for the wrapper repo.
- Use `git pull` inside each relevant `apps/<name>` repo.
- Use `node bin/maiw.js ensure <name>` or `/maiw sync <name>` when memory freshness also needs to be
  reconciled.
